  "description": "<p>Currently, Fedora 6 treats the value of the Slug header as an un-encoded string. However, per the spec, it should be treated as a url encoded value.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora.info/2018/11/22/spec/#http-post\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora.info/2018/11/22/spec/#http-post</a><br/>\n<a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/ldp/#h-ldpc-post-slug\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://www.w3.org/TR/ldp/#h-ldpc-post-slug</a><br/>\n<a href=\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5023#section-9.7\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5023#section-9.7</a></p>\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\necho <span class=\"code-quote\">\"hello world\"</span> | curl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/ -H<span class=\"code-quote\">'Link: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#NonRDFSource&gt;; rel=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"type\"</span>'</span> -H<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Slug: %C3%A4bc3\"</span> --data-binary @- -XPOST -v</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>Should create the resource \"äbc3\", but it actually creates the resource \"%C3%A4bc3\"</p>",
